## What actually passed and where execution stopped

[Native run 34359447892](https://github.com/saidi19/lumi-model/actions/runs/34359447892),
attempt 1, job `102492361796`, ran on the exact published source. The corrected
source/synthetic preflight passed. Acquisition and hash verification of the
already accepted software also passed: four HTTPS GET attempts, zero retries,
1,062,113,436-byte ZIP and 1,062,113,280-byte software tar, both matching the
unchanged v0.62/v0.63 pins. No large software artifact was downloaded on the Mac.

The native step started at 13:49:33Z and stopped at 13:49:59Z. Its report says
`status=failed`, `stage=inspect_container`, `code=fixture_failed`. This is the
first `verify_created_oci` call, which includes both image and container checks;
it does not establish that the actual container-inspect command was reached.
Source ordering establishes that load/create completed and that export,
extraction, adapter installation, workload cgroups and all three worker cases
were **not reached**. No container was started. No worker, GPU, model/data
access, inference or SFT was started.

The separate input-retirement step passed and attests removal of exactly one
owned temporary input file and its directory. Root fixture control flow did not
report `cleanup_unconfirmed`, but the failure report has no explicit root
cleanup attestation or independently retained final Docker inventory. Do not
upgrade the input-cleanup receipt into a broader cleanup claim.

