## Confirmed reporting defect; native cause still unknown

The guardian fixture's `main` preserves only exact `FixtureError` codes.
`verify_created_oci` raises a different exact type, `OciAdmissionError`, so all
its fixed codes are flattened to `fixture_failed`. Merely wrapping its code in
`FixtureError` would still lose most codes: the fixture's allowlist excludes
them. A safe correction needs explicit typed, fixed-code mapping or a separate
allowlisted `admission_code` field, never arbitrary exception attributes/text.

Read-only independent source review confirmed this reporting defect. It cannot
identify the native failing predicate. The failed call covers runtime and
deadline validation, inspect transport/JSON, image identity, container state,
host profile and configuration equivalence. Even `profile_rejected` alone
would not identify the individual predicate. No parser/profile relaxation or
speculative null/empty normalization is justified by the retained evidence.

