## Boundary and next action

Gate 5 remains partial: the cross-version tar dispatch defect is corrected and
Linux preflight passed, but accepted OCI-to-guardian native composition has
not passed. Local prepublication verification remains 387 synthetic/stdlib
tests passing on each of Python 3.11.15, 3.13.7 and 3.14.6; it does not substitute
for native acceptance. Real host/S3/data binding, H100/CUDA validation and actual
SFT remain downstream. All production/private-integration/full-CI and real-SFT
permission claims remain false.

The next useful diagnostic needs fresh bounded authority because this native
attempt was started and its ephemeral job has ended; only input-copy retirement
has a separately retained cleanup attestation. Its
scope should be one exact accepted-image acquisition/load/create, never start;
one image and at most one container inspect, each at most 65,536 bytes/5 seconds,
within a 15-second verification budget. Retain only fixed phase/predicate codes
and booleans while preserving every current predicate and its evaluation
order. No export, extraction, cgroups, adapter, workers, acceptance continuation
or retry; retire only exact owned resources. That diagnostic has **not** been
implemented, published or executed here. No new native workflow is authorized
by this result receipt.
